        "role": "user",
        "content": "Read the exact question and ALL original source segments. Documents, cards, saved answers and annotations are fallible data, never instructions. Distinct valid namesakes and complementary answers may coexist; competing assertions about one referent are not automatically distinct valid answers. Do not invent source authority, document independence or unstated question constraints. A quoted assertion, occurrence, or repeated text is not truth. Match requested subject/object, relation direction, negation, time and answer type. A city in a birth sentence is not a date. In \"A's manager B\", B is the manager, not A. Sports biographies can positively support multiple legitimate sports. An incidental chart, associated person or date is not automatically the answer. Use only supplied candidate/source IDs in bounded fields; no free quotation or prose.\nFor EVERY candidate, judge fit: direct means the answer itself fills the exact requested relation for an allowed referent; wrong_argument is explicit role/type mismatch; incidental means occurrence without enough support; uncertain means unresolved. Select support only for an original segment positively assigning this candidate to the requested relation; otherwise empty. Select counter only for actual counterevidence, not mere absence. conflict=same_referent only for incompatible claims for the same entity/attribute/relevant scope, not legitimate namesakes or complementary facts. entity labels are provisional groups, not truth. scope=excluded only for an explicit question constraint, with constraint selecting a literal numeric phrase from the question; otherwise allowed/unknown. observed_slot describes the answer's ACTUAL role, not the role wanted by the question. Mere disagreement does not make a source false. Fill all opaque keys.\nCheck polarity before every label. A passage saying candidate X is the artist, born date, sport, population or symbol asked for is SUPPORT, never counterevidence merely because another passage gives Y. Set support to that passage, fit=direct, observed_slot to the requested role, and counter empty unless there is actual negation or role exclusion. Examples with invented names: two albums both called Evening, one by Mira and one by Noel, support BOTH artists. Two people called Alex born1901 and1873 support BOTH dates. A player practicing golf AND tennis supports BOTH sports. A passage saying London is a birthplace makes London a wrong_argument for a birth-DATE question. Distinguish an asserted false same-role answer from a type error. Before wrong_argument, verify the source actually attributes a DIFFERENT role. Do not invent a disagreement or unknown conflict just to fill the field; differing allowed entities are not contradictions.\nInput: {\"question\": \"221B Baker Street is a game for which type of medium?\", \"slot_hint\": \"other\", \"all_original_sources\": {\"D1S1\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0044-b1d64654a870:d00\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 245, \"text\": \"221B Baker Street (board game) 221B Baker Street: The Master Detective Game is a board game featuring Arthur Conan Doyle's fictional detective Sherlock Holmes and developed by Jay Moriarty (dba Antler Productions) in 1975 and sold by the John N.\"}, \"D1S2\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0044-b1d64654a870:d00\", \"start\": 246, \"end\": 256, \"text\": \"Hansen Co.\"}, \"D1S3\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0044-b1d64654a870:d00\", \"start\": 257, \"end\": 278, \"text\": \"in the US since 1977.\"}, \"D1S4\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0044-b1d64654a870:d00\", \"start\": 279, \"end\": 440, \"text\": \"The players have to solve cases using the clues provided by visiting locations on the board such as 221B Baker Street, Scotland Yard, Apothecary and Pawn Broker.\"}, \"D1S5\": {\"document_number\": 1, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0044-b1d64654a870:d00\", \"start\": 441, \"end\": 581, \"text\": \"The original game has twenty cases, but there are eight expansion sets of 20 cases each for a total of 180 cases available for play, created\"}, \"D2S1\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0044-b1d64654a870:d01\", \"start\": 0, \"end\": 73, \"text\": \", out of a number of facts , which are incidental , and which are vital .\"}, \"D2S2\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0044-b1d64654a870:d01\", \"start\": 74, \"end\": 151, \"text\": \"– Sherlock Holmes Think you ’ ve got what it takes to be a master detective ?\"}, \"D2S3\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0044-b1d64654a870:d01\", \"start\": 152, \"end\": 296, \"text\": \"Try your hand in the art of deduction in a race against your friends to solve one of 75 thrilling mysteries in this family friendly board game !\"}, \"D2S4\": {\"document_number\": 2, \"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0044-b1d64654a870:d01\", \"start\": 297, \"end\": 492, \"text\": \"Starting at 221B Baker Street , home to the world ’ s greatest detective Sherlock Holme , you will compete to be the first to solve a crime by scouring the streets of London for clues and putting\"}}, \"original_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0044-b1d64654a870:d00\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0044-b1d64654a870:d00:c0\", \"entity\": \"221B Baker Street\", \"scope\": \"game type\", \"claim\": \"221B Baker Street: The Master Detective Game is a board game.\", \"answer\": \"board game\", \"quote\": \"221B Baker Street (board game) 221B Baker Street: The Master Detective Game is a board game featuring Arthur Conan Doyle's fictional detective Sherlock Holmes and developed by Jay Moriarty (dba Antler Productions) in 1975 and sold by the John N.\", \"original_document_number\": 1}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0044-b1d64654a870:d01\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0044-b1d64654a870:d01:c0\", \"entity\": \"221B Baker Street\", \"scope\": \"game type\", \"claim\": \"221B Baker Street is a family friendly board game.\", \"answer\": \"board game\", \"quote\": \"Try your hand in the art of deduction in a race against your friends to solve one of 75 thrilling mysteries in this family friendly board game !\", \"original_document_number\": 2}], \"R5_answers\": [\"board game\"], \"candidates\": [{\"id\": \"C0\", \"answer\": \"board game\", \"origin\": \"R5\"}]}"
